= MSH Reader 3.0 =

#type: node
#context: sop
#internal: MSH_Reader::3.0
#tags: gmsh, msh, tetrahedra, hexahedra, mesh, import

"""Reads a Gmsh .msh mesh (versions 2.2 and 4.1, text or binary) into Houdini, with its physical groups."""

== Overview ==

The file is parsed directly; nothing needs to be installed. The mesh's
highest dimension becomes the primary elements: tetrahedra and hexahedra for
a volume mesh, triangles and quadrilaterals for a 2D mesh, lines for a 1D
mesh. The PolyFEM node uses this node to load its meshes.

== Attributes ==

:: `msh_pt_id` (point):
    The node's tag in the file.
:: `msh_physical_tag` (primitive):
    The element's physical group tag as written in the file (0 = the element
    is in no physical group).
:: `Entity` (primitive):
    The physical tag, plus 1 for every element when any element has no
    group (the convention of MSH Reader 2.2, kept for compatibility). The
    PolyFEM node numbers its subdomains from `msh_physical_tag` instead:
    sorted tags, elements without a group last.
:: `msh_physical_names` (detail):
    The file's `$PhysicalNames` for the primary dimension, as JSON
    (`{"tag": "name"}`).
:: `is_volume`, `ElementNum`, `centroid` (primitive):
    Whether the primitive is a primary element, its sequential number, and
    its centroid.
:: `surface_entity` (primitive):
    With __Import Physical Surfaces__, the physical tag of 2D groups in a 3D
    mesh (loaded as polygons, e.g. to see Gmsh-authored sidesets).

== More ==

* [Feature guide (docs/hdas.md)|https://github.com/sdast9/houdini-plugins/blob/main/docs/hdas.md]
* [Gmsh MSH file format|https://gmsh.info/doc/texinfo/gmsh.html#MSH-file-format]

@parameters

MSH File:
    The `.msh` file to load.

Reload:
    Read the file again (after re-meshing with the same name).

Import Physical Surfaces:
    For a 3D mesh, also load 2D physical groups as polygons with a
    `surface_entity` attribute.
